{{! brief.md.tmpl: the single brief template. `keel brief <P|P.Tn> --seat <seat>` and every dispatch render
  it from the brief IR through the logic-less Mustache subset keel uses: values, sections that repeat per
  item or render once when true, inverted sections that render when empty or false, and dropped comments
  like this one. No HTML escaping. The JSON companion is schemas/brief.schema.json.

  Regions:
  - header: brief id, stamps, freshness and section input hashes. Not hashed.
  - body: between the keel:brief:body markers. BR-<sha12> is the sha256 of the body after LF, BOM and
    NFC normalization; the same bytes go through every channel, and the golden hash is identical on a
    Windows CRLF checkout and on Linux. Each level-2 heading is one brief section; its id from
    schemas/brief.schema.json is given in the header's hash list.
  - The runtime wrapper (a fixed short instruction, an agent-file frontmatter) is added by the runtime
    templates outside this file and is never hashed.

  The compiler selects slices: the why-chain, covered requirements and ACC, INV and obligations whose
  applies_to intersects the write set, the element brief and impact. Sections with no slice for this
  seat and subject are omitted. A review packet never contains the engineer's transcript or rationale;
  the intent-alignment packet holds only the frozen intent and the diff.
  Budget: per runtime profile. ACC items and must and must_not obligations are never truncated; an over-budget brief
  means the task must be split. Nothing here may carry a provider value; records use env NAMES only. }}
